      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-5261",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/problem",
          "value": "Given that $2 - 3 \\textrm{i} = \\dfrac{p - 2q \\textrm{i} }{1 + 2 \\textrm{i}},$ calculate $p$ and $q.$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/example-5261.json",
          "file_sha256": "e9ab835868a153395504f7236a75a77c7c12b382f412de0d9be0d17c97c1c4b6"
        }
      ],
      "basis": 1522,
      "reason": "Observed MA content supersedes the stored value",
      "action": "replace",
      "transaction_receipt": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/edb-import/commit.edn",
      "basis_after": 1523
    },
    {
      "question": "e-5261",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "dbf88236108c15e2d24c7d4e2ff7df8efdb42b8691845d19e65d2f8eab79cdc6",
      "new_sha256": "8a0230912ac6338a0e684f8acbcf4f39a6f1e3a57cfb4793f09e29e032e6eb68",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-5261",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $1+2\\textrm{i}$ to get rid of the fraction and isolate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2-3\\text{i} & =\\frac{p-2q\\text{i}}{1+2\\text{i}} \\\\ (2-3\\text{i})(1+2\\text{i}) & =p-2q\\text{i} \\\\ 2+4\\text{i}-3\\text{i}-6{\\text{i}}^{2} & =p-2q\\text{i} \\\\ 2+\\text{i}-6(-1) & =p-2q\\text{i} \\\\ 8+\\text{i} & =p-2q\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get\n\n$$\n8 = p.\n$$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =-2q \\\\ q & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=8$ and $q = -\\dfrac{1}{2}.$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/example-5261.json",
          "file_sha256": "e9ab835868a153395504f7236a75a77c7c12b382f412de0d9be0d17c97c1c4b6"
        }
      ],
